{"packet_id":"D040-01","doc_id":"D040","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Just Cause for Eviction Ordinance (JCO)","requirement":"A landlord may not terminate a tenancy without just cause; at-fault causes include non-payment, nuisance and lease violations, while no-fault causes such as owner move-in or demolition require relocation assistance. Eviction notices must be filed with LAHD within three business days.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Most residential properties in the City of Los Angeles not regulated by the City's RSO, where the tenant has lived in the unit at least six months or the original lease expired. Applies to buildings newer than October 1, 1978.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Can apply to buildings newer than October 1, 1978 and to a property with only one single-family dwelling; tenant must have 6 months in the unit or an expired lease."},"exemptions":"Transient hotels, licensed care facilities, fraternity or sorority houses, owner's roommate, cooperatives under certain circumstances, some non-profit facilities for the homeless or short-term substance-abuse treatment centers, and some properties owned by HACLA or the government.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"City of Los Angeles Just Cause for Eviction Ordinance (JCO)","quoted_span":"If you own rental property in the City of Los Angeles, it may be subject to the Just Cause Ordinance (JCO).  It prohibits terminations of tenancies without just cause and requires relocation assistance for no-fault evictions.","interaction":"The JCO does not regulate rent increases; state law AB 1482 may regulate the rent amount in buildings older than 15 years.","confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D040-01","doc_id":"D040","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Non-payment of rent eviction protection (Fair Market Rent threshold)","requirement":"For all RSO and JCO rental units, a landlord may not evict a tenant who falls behind in rent unless the tenant owes an amount higher than the Fair Market Rent for the unit's bedroom size.","key_value":"Arrears must exceed Fair Market Rent","coverage_conditions":"Applies to all RSO and JCO rental units in the City of Los Angeles; the FMR threshold depends on the bedroom size of the rental unit.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2023-03-27","citation":"LAHD, Just Cause For Eviction Ordinance (JCO) – Evictions for Non-Payment of Rent","quoted_span":"Applies to all RSO & JCO rental units. Effective March 27, 2023, landlords may not evict a tenant who falls behind in rent unless the tenant owes an amount higher than the Fair Market Rent (FMR).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D040-01","doc_id":"D040","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California Tenant Protection Act (AB 1482) annual rent cap","requirement":"Annual rent increases for covered units are limited to no more than 5% plus the percentage change in the regional cost of living, or 10%, whichever is lower. The maximum allowable increase was 8.9% from August 1, 2024 to July 31, 2025.","key_value":"5% + CPI, max 10%; 8.9% (Aug 1, 2024–Jul 31, 2025)","coverage_conditions":"Buildings older than 15 years, applied on a rolling basis. Single-family homes and condominiums are covered only if not owned by a trust, corporation, or LLC with a corporate member and the required written notice was given.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":"construction_date","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Coverage is rolling: a unit becomes covered 15 years after construction; two-unit owner-occupied property, certain dormitories, deed-restricted affordable units and RSO units exempt."},"exemptions":"Units constructed within the last 15 years; units deed- or regulatory-restricted to low or moderate income; certain dormitories; a two-unit property where the owner occupied the second unit for the entire tenancy; qualifying single-family homes and condominiums; units already subject to the City's RSO.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-08-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1947.12","quoted_span":"Effective August 1, 2024 to July 31, 2025, the maximum allowable increase is 8.9%. Previously, from August 1, 2023 to July 31, 2024 the maximum annual increase for units subject to AB 1482 was 8.8%","interaction":"The City's JCO does not regulate rent increases; units already subject to the City's RSO are exempt from this state cap.","confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
